name: Telecom bypass (SIM-box)
tagline: "SIM-box signals from voice CDRs - a daily per-SIM feature Dataset of twelve signals, over a synthetic corpus"
description: "A bypass / SIM-box detection content pack (slice B1 of the plan: signals only). One voice CDR feed with optional device and call-outcome columns, three small Reference feeds (cell sites, own number ranges, the subscriber profile), and one daily sql.template Job, tb_features, that writes one row per SIM per day with twelve CDR-derivable signals (B-number diversity, call shape, answer rate, inbound share, service mix, cells and implied speed, sequential dialling, hour profile, burst cadence, overlapping calls, own-network targets, tenure and activation batch) plus a box_like flag from five configurable clauses. A signal whose optional column or Reference is absent is omitted and named in the missing column; it never fails the Job. It scores nothing and raises no Alert yet: the Risk Score, the Entity Lists, the Alert Rules and the box-level Incident arrive in the next slices. A CDR pattern is evidence of consistency with a box, never proof. Every threshold is configuration and illustrative until calibrated on the operator's own traffic. Needs the Standard, Advanced or Preview edition."
minEdition: standard
icon: heroicons_outline:signal-slash
contents[6]: "4 Pipelines + schemas (voice CDR, cell sites, number plan, subscriber profile)", "1 daily SIM-day feature Job (sql.template): twelve signals and the box_like flag", "5 Datasets (4 feeds, 1 Job-written)", "Zero-row schema seeds", "Runbook skeleton", "Example SLA policies and Escalation Rules (inert)"
